WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.559
The antibody reaches the tumour. In an advertisement

00:00:03.559 --> 00:00:07.445
that would be the triumphant final shot. In an ADC,

00:00:07.445 --> 00:00:09.388
chemistry is just getting started.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.943
An antibody-drug conjugate is a chemical system. Tumour

00:00:20.943 --> 00:00:25.310
binding is only one step in an exposure and release

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:25.747
problem.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:35.411
Stable, cleavable and non-cleavable linkers change what

00:00:35.411 --> 00:00:39.218
escapes the carrier, how much reaches other tissues and

00:00:39.218 --> 00:00:41.333
how a tumour is exposed.

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:51.196
Drug-to-antibody ratio influences distribution,

00:00:51.196 --> 00:00:55.314
heterogeneity and pharmacokinetics. Higher loading is

00:00:55.314 --> 00:00:58.059
not automatically more precise.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:08.052
Even a stable linker may deliver a drug class

00:01:08.052 --> 00:01:11.119
associated with specific toxicities, including serious

00:01:11.119 --> 00:01:13.165
complications outside the tumour.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:21.731
Internalisation, linker behaviour and payload transport

00:01:21.731 --> 00:01:26.106
determine where exposure occurs. Binding alone does not

00:01:26.106 --> 00:01:28.294
settle safety or efficacy.

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:35.563
Permeable payloads may help reach heterogeneous

00:01:35.563 --> 00:01:39.195
tumours, but surrounding normal tissue and exposure

00:01:39.195 --> 00:01:41.270
constrain the apparent advantage.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:49.915
An antibody–drug conjugate is an engineered

00:01:49.915 --> 00:01:53.380
pharmacological system whose components must succeed

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:53.957
together.
